# MODULE AP — EMPLOYEE SELF-SERVICE INTEGRATION

Integrate Phase 12 with Phase 11 ESS.

Employees should be able to access:

My Compliance Information

My Documents

My Policy Acknowledgements

My Consent

My Data Requests

My Certifications

My Statutory Profile

My Expiring Documents

However:

Employees must NEVER be able to access another employee's sensitive compliance data.

---

# MODULE AQ — MANAGER INTEGRATION

Managers should see only permitted compliance information.

Examples:

* Team compliance warnings
* Missing documents
* Expiring certifications
* Attendance compliance alerts
* Overtime threshold warnings

Do NOT expose sensitive tax/social-security identifiers to managers by default.

---

# MODULE AR — HR ADMIN INTEGRATION

HR administrators should be able to:

* Manage employee statutory records
* Monitor compliance
* Manage registrations
* Manage documents
* Review violations
* Manage policy acknowledgements
* Run reports
* Handle employee privacy requests where authorized

---

# MODULE AS — PAYROLL INTEGRATION

Compliance must integrate with the existing payroll engine.

Before payroll finalization, support checks such as:

* Applicable tax configuration exists
* Employee statutory profile complete
* Required contribution configuration exists
* Minimum wage validation
* Overtime compliance
* Required deductions configured
* Required registration configuration
* Effective-dated rule availability

Payroll should be able to produce:

COMPLIANCE_CHECK_PASSED

or

COMPLIANCE_CHECK_FAILED

or

COMPLIANCE_CHECK_WARNING

Do not silently change payroll values.

---

# MODULE AT — PRE-PAYROLL COMPLIANCE VALIDATION

Create a pre-payroll compliance validation engine.

Example:

POST

/api/v1/compliance/payroll/precheck

Return:

* Errors
* Warnings
* Affected employees
* Rules triggered
* Recommended actions

Example:

Employee 1023

Issue:
Applicable minimum wage rule violated.

Severity:
HIGH

Action:
Review compensation configuration.

---

# MODULE AU — POST-PAYROLL COMPLIANCE VALIDATION

After payroll processing:

Validate:

* Tax calculations
* Contributions
* Statutory deductions
* Employer contributions
* Minimum wage
* Overtime
* Payroll totals
* Compliance rules

Store validation results.

Never modify historical payroll silently.

---

# MODULE AV — COMPLIANCE SNAPSHOTS

Create compliance snapshots.

A snapshot represents the compliance state at a particular point in time.

Fields:

snapshot_id
tenant_id
snapshot_date
calculation_version
compliance_score
open_violations
overdue_tasks
expiring_documents
risk_level

This supports historical reporting and audits.

---

# MODULE AW — MULTI-TENANT SECURITY

This is mandatory.

Every compliance entity must be tenant-scoped.

Never allow:

Tenant A

to access:

Tenant B

data.

Use existing tenant isolation architecture.

Validate tenant ownership at:

* API
* Service
* Repository
* Database query
* File access
* Report generation

Do not rely only on frontend filtering.

---

# MODULE AX — RBAC

Extend existing RBAC.

Potential permissions:

compliance.view
compliance.create
compliance.update
compliance.delete
compliance.approve
compliance.manage_rules
compliance.manage_registrations
compliance.manage_tasks
compliance.manage_violations
compliance.manage_audits
compliance.view_reports
compliance.export
compliance.manage_privacy
compliance.manage_retention
compliance.manage_legal_hold
compliance.manage_statutory_data

Do not automatically grant these permissions to all administrators.

---

# MODULE AY — FIELD-LEVEL SECURITY

Sensitive fields require stronger controls.

Examples:

* Tax identifiers
* Social-security identifiers
* Bank-related compliance information
* Legal documents
* Employee statutory information

Implement masking.

Example:

Full value:

XXXXXXXX1234

Authorized user:

FULL_VALUE

Unauthorized user:

********1234

Where appropriate, implement access logging for sensitive field access.

---

# MODULE AZ — AUDIT LOGGING

Every sensitive compliance action must generate an audit record.

Track:

* Actor
* Tenant
* Action
* Resource
* Resource ID
* Timestamp
* IP
* User agent
* Old value where safe
* New value where safe
* Reason
* Result

Examples:

RULE_CREATED

RULE_UPDATED

RULE_APPROVED

REGISTRATION_CREATED

REGISTRATION_UPDATED

DOCUMENT_ACCESSED

DOCUMENT_DOWNLOADED

STATUTORY_PROFILE_UPDATED

