# 19. API SECURITY

Protect every endpoint.

Validate:

Authentication

Tenant

Permission

Resource ownership

Manager scope

Employee scope

Field-level access

Input validation

File access

Pagination

Sorting

Filtering

Export authorization

Never trust:

employee_id
tenant_id
organization_id
user_id

from the frontend without server-side validation.

For `/me` APIs, resolve identity from the authenticated session/token.

---

# 20. IDOR PROTECTION

Explicitly test:

Tenant A user requesting Tenant B compliance rule.

Employee A requesting Employee B statutory profile.

Manager requesting another department's compliance data.

Unauthorized HR user requesting payroll compliance details.

User changing IDs in URL/query parameters.

Every case must return an appropriate authorization error.

---

# 21. RATE LIMITING

Protect sensitive endpoints:

* Privacy requests
* Document downloads
* Compliance exports
* Search
* Authentication-related endpoints
* Sensitive data access

Reuse the existing rate-limiting architecture.

---

# 22. REPORT EXPORT SECURITY

Exports can contain highly sensitive data.

Therefore:

* Permission required
* Audit every export
* Record export type
* Record actor
* Record filters
* Record timestamp
* Avoid logging sensitive data
* Restrict export columns by role

